cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use repository-authored InclusiveShift-HAR software, cite this
  metadata and cite every third-party dataset separately under its own terms.
title: >-
  InclusiveShift-HAR: A Leakage-Safe Benchmark for Physical-Ability
  Generalization in Smartphone Activity Recognition
type: software
version: 0.1.0a0
authors:
  - family-names: Huseyinli
    given-names: Abdulla
abstract: >-
  Research software for leakage-safe, participant-exclusive evaluation of
  ability-associated population shift in smartphone inertial human activity
  recognition. The benchmark and proposed MoRe-HAR model are provisional;
  this metadata does not assert confirmatory results, fairness, clinical
  validity, state-of-the-art performance, or publication status.
keywords:
  - human activity recognition
  - wearable sensing
  - inertial sensors
  - domain generalization
  - participant-exclusive evaluation
  - reproducible research
license: Apache-2.0
notes: >-
  Apache-2.0 applies only to repository-authored material that the copyright
  holder has authority to license. Third-party datasets, legacy coursework
  artifacts, checkpoints, papers, and figures retain their original terms.
